**Plan: branch in `cli.js`, print `buildRows()` as JSON.** No new module needed.

```js
const flags = argv.slice(1);
const json = flags.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

One call to make: the table drops `owner` and `slow`. `[format.js:3](src/format.js:3)` says a caller wanting the whole row goes back to `buildRows()`. So JSON prints all six fields. Say the word if you want the four table columns instead.

Also updating `USAGE` at `[cli.js:6](src/cli.js:6)` and rejecting unknown flags.
